# sshd_config — hardened directives only
#
# This is an EXCERPT, not the full file. Append these lines to your
# existing /etc/ssh/sshd_config (or merge with what's already there),
# don't just drop this in as a replacement.
#
# On newer Ubuntu releases, SSH may use socket activation (ssh.socket)
# rather than binding its port directly from sshd_config. If changing
# `Port` here has no effect, see HARDENING.md for the systemd override
# fix that was needed on this server.

Port 2222
PermitRootLogin no
PasswordAuthentication no

AllowTcpForwarding no
AllowAgentForwarding no
X11Forwarding no
TCPKeepAlive no

MaxAuthTries 3
MaxSessions 2
ClientAliveCountMax 2

LogLevel VERBOSE
Banner /etc/issue.net
